1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,160
Imagine you fall into a
black hole, feet first.

2
00:00:03,545 --> 00:00:04,515
What would you feel?

3
00:00:05,617 --> 00:00:08,627
Gravity pulls much harder on
your feet than on your head.

4
00:00:08,877 --> 00:00:10,867
So your body is stretched long and thin.

5
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:14,087
At the same time,
your sides are squeezed inward.

6
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,420
Scientists call this spaghettification.

7
00:00:17,725 --> 00:00:19,855
Stephen Hawking made the word famous.

8
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:23,500
The size of the black
hole changes everything.

9
00:00:23,785 --> 00:00:27,415
A small one stretches you apart
before you even reach its edge.

10
00:00:27,635 --> 00:00:31,665
A giant one lets you cross the
edge without feeling much at all.

11
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:36,020
A friend watching from far
away sees something strange.

12
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,150
You seem to slow down near the edge.

13
00:00:38,415 --> 00:00:41,365
You look redder and dimmer,
until you fade from view.

14
00:00:42,383 --> 00:00:45,073
Once you cross the edge,
there is no way back.

15
00:00:45,363 --> 00:00:48,353
Nothing, not even light,
can escape from inside.

